AB  - 81 members of a self-help group for obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD) patients completed a questionnaire on psychological problems, biographical data, and the family and social context of OCD. The mean duration of Ss' OCD was 18 yrs, and 74% of the Ss rated their symptoms as severe for 50% of the time since onset. Ss rated behavior therapy and psychotherapy as the most effective treatments. Employed females reported significantly fewer obsessional symptoms than did unemployed females. High scores on measures of perceived parental protection correlated signficantly with the amount of treatment received. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
