AB  - In a study examining whether substance abuse patients self-selecting into one of three aftercare groups (outpatient treatment only, 12-step groups only, & outpatient treatment & 12-step groups) & patients who did not participate in aftercare differed on 1-year substance use & psychosocial outcomes, a total of 3,018 male patients at a Veterans Affairs hospital completed a questionnaire at intake & 1 year following discharge from treatment. Patients who participated in both outpatient treatment & 12-step groups, especially those who participated the most frequently, fared the best on 1-year outcomes. Encouraging substance abuse patients to regularly attend both outpatient aftercare & self-help groups may improve long-term outcomes. 4 Tables, 37 References. Adapted from the source document.
