AB  - A program in Lexington, KY, designed to meet the judicial needs of the state & to provide comprehensive mental health services to felony-convicted juvenile offenders on intensive probation is described. The theoretical emphasis of the program is the dysfunctional process of separation-individuation experienced by juvenile offenders. The program relied on group interactions to promote respect & adherence to group rules, & to decrease acting out behavior. The following group goals emerged: (1) increase in self-awareness; (2) taking responsibility for one's own behavior; (3) development of understanding of impact of environment on personal development; & (4) increase in hopefulness. Cooperation between nurse therapist & probation officer was integral to the program. Specific therapeutic interventions & barriers are presented. 8 References. Adapted from the source document.
