AB  - ; The article presents information on personality factors related to participation treatment by hospitalized male alcoholics. 50 hospitalized, male alcoholics were studied for relationships between personality characteristics and voluntary participation in Alcoholics Anonymous (AA) meetings, group therapy and request for Disulfiram or conditioned-reflex treatment. There was a positive relationship between authoritarian attitudes and attendance at AA, and a positive relationship between conscious acceptance of the drinking problem and attendance at group therapy or request for Disulfiram. Subjects who showed less autism, paranoid thinking or withdrawal tendencies tended to accept all forms of treatment, but particularly group therapy and Disulfiram.
