AB  - This article focuses on the treatment of alcoholism. People who are dependent on alcohol have high rates of co-occurring psychiatric disorders as well. Elevated rates of antisocial personality disorder, major depression, anxiety disorders, bipolar disorder, and schizophrenia are found among alcohol abusers. Several promising avenues have been identified for the treatment of alcohol abuse and alcoholism as they occur with anxiety, depression, bipolar disorder and schizophrenia. The authors conclude that the introduction of social reinforcement into aftercare group therapy increased clients' frequency and duration of aftercare attendance.
