AB  - Evaluated the frequency and patterns of alcohol use and alcohol-related problems among 404 adult male alcoholics admitted to a psychiatric treatment center. 102 of the Ss had personality disorders. Alcoholics were offered a socio-medical treatment program, and treatment outcome was evaluated 1 yr after admission. Data show that alcohol abuse was specifically related to antisocial personality, and marked differences in treatment outcome were found among personality disorders (e.g., histrionic, compulsive). Group therapy for alcoholism was not beneficial to antisocial personalities, but was useful among Ss with dependent personalities. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
