AB  - This article presents a case study that considers a particular self-help mutual-aid group: Alcoholics Anonymous. On the empirical level, the research is conducted through the participant observation method. Starting from a brief analysis of these types of associations, both from the point of view of their evolution & from the point of view of the sociologists, the author tries to analyze how the Twelve Steps groups specifically work & what their cure method consists of. This study aims at demonstrating how the recovery method used in these groups (& in general in all groups that use Twelve Step Programs) could be considered, to every extent, an effective alternative therapy. Adapted from the source document.
