AB  - Studied the prevalence of psychiatric disorders among drug abusers in therapeutic community (TC) treatment. Psychiatric diagnoses based on Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM-III) criteria were obtained with the Diagnostic Interview Schedule on a sample of 58 Ss entering Phoenix House residential treatment in 1985 in New York, New York. Results indicate the presence of psychopathological signs among drug abusers who seek treatment, although there is little evidence of psychosis or severe psychiatric disorder. Substance abuse is viewed as a prominent element in a psychological profile that contains features from both psychiatric and criminal populations. Implications for TC admissions criteria, treatment of drug abusers, and psychiatric diagnosis are noted. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
