AB  - Examined 36 adult substance abusers at intake and after 1 yr of residency in a hierarchical therapeutic community, using the Millon Clinical Multiaxial Inventory (MCMI), a basic character inventory, and the SCL-90. Two antisocial aggressiveness subgroups were identified. The no-increase group of 11 Ss had high intake scores on MCMI antisocial aggression, small changes during the stay, and a high dropout rate (45%) as outpatients. The increase group consisted of 25 Ss who had lower scores at intake and a low dropout rate, but whose scores increased during the 1-yr inpatient phase. A high level of antisocial aggressiveness at intake was related to dropout in the no-increase group, and a high degree of increase in antisocial aggressiveness was related to dropout in the increase group. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
