AB  - This paper examines the relationship between the concepts of individual & collective trauma, assesses how they are evaluated, & presents some alternatives of psychosocial work within the context of full & complete reparation. The following reflections are the result of work carried out in the reparation & assistance area of the National Commission for Reparation & Recuperation. The article concludes by underlining the importance of psychosocial initiatives in areas of long-standing armed conflict & emphasizing the need to deal with the trauma of violence, which helps communities make sense of events in order to promote the healing effects of the process & reduce the psychosocial vulnerability that such events repeat themselves. Adapted from the source document.
