AB  - The article offers information related to mental health law in the U.S. It says that the study conducted by Tanya Wanchek shows that the extension of temporary detention order (TDO) periods under Virginia law could improve the health outcomes of individuals experiencing mental health crises such as lower probability of hospitalization. It mentions that the survey by the Joint Commission on Health Care and the Commission on Mental Health Law Reform indicates that 70% students are served by counseling centers in private colleges than in public colleges. It adds that the United States Supreme Court has ordered California to decrease its prison population to deliver adequate treatment for mental and medical conditions of inmates with serious mental illness.
