AB  - The article provides an overview of the psychosocial issues, interventions and implications, and lessons learned pertaining to the situation of Bhutanese refugees in refugee camps in eastern Nepal. Psychosocial issues confronting Bhutanese refugees are discussed including contextual stressors related to basic needs, shelter and resettlement opportunities, the problem of suicides, and substance abuse. The psychosocial care programme is presented along with challenges to psychosocial counselling. INSET: Case study: an example of a psychosocial intervention.
