AB  - In this chapter, we describe how 12-step groups can be tailored for use with patients with eating disorders. We provide some brief background information about the 12-step philosophy of Alcoholics Anonymous (AA). We also describe how we adapt the 12-step philosophy for the treatment of eating disorders in our inpatient and residential programs. On the basis of our clinical experience and the writings of other professionals, we discuss potential concerns and benefits of 12-step groups and offer some general recommendations for implementing such groups in an ethical and effective manner. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
