AB  - This case study attempts to investigate the effectiveness of functional treatment strategies on the acquisition, development and refinement of socialization, communication and independent living skills for people dually diagnosed with mental retardation and psychiatric disorders. Subjects were exposed to functional treatment through small group, community based instruction. Review of the data suggested no statistically significant difference through the use of the t test for non-independent samples but some individuals did evidence gains in age equivalent scores on the Vineland Adaptive Behavior Scales - Expanded Form. Implications for future directions in research are offered. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
