AB  - The field of psychiatric rehabilitation in Israel has developed rapidly in recent years. The Rehabilitation of Psychiatrically Disabled Persons in the Community Act 2000 mandates the provision of a rudimentary set of services to persons who meet criteria for eligibility, and the number of individuals who receive those services has been steadily increasing. However, because the legislation does not define explicit criteria for choosing the intervention methods, there are no official standards and guidelines for assessing the merits of the methods or the effectiveness of their implementation. In this article, we argue that psychiatric rehabilitation interventions vary in their effectiveness, and that evaluation of effectiveness is essential for ensuring the quality of services. Toward that end, we focus on recent efforts to identify and implement evidence-based psychiatric rehabilitation interventions.
