AB  - Certain clinical features of depression in men led us to develop a specific group intervention: higher incidence of successful suicide, greater reluctance to seek professional treatment, tendency to isolate themselves and use of drugs to relieve the suffering. In this work we report the clinical improvement of six patients diagnosed with chronic major depression after two years of group psychotherapy. This treatment is based on Interpersonal Psychotherapy. The psychometric instruments used were: MADRS (assesses the intensity of depressive symptoms), SDI (perceived disability in different areas) and CGI-SI (clinical impression). The results show improvement in all areas. Our experience in this group psychotherapy programme highlights the relevance of specific and long- term treatment for the prevention of relapses. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
