AB  - The article deals with the assertive training program, which was developed to increase social skills and competence. People lead isolated life because of lack of social competence. It is a problem of large portion of the population. Lack of social competence is often a part of other problems such as alcoholism, sexual dilemmas, absenteeism from school and work, depression, and loneliness. The article presents a study that teaches its clients to develop conversational ability. It teaches its clients to say "no" more often when appropriate, use the telephone, make social visits, have dates, use facial expression more effectively, and increase or control the manifestation of appropriate feeling. As a person gains greater social competence and learns to be appropriately assertive, there is evidence that his anxiety is reduced. It is assertive approach. It stresses on the importance of the group treatment and to treat clients in the group, one by one as individual patients would of course fail to utilize the group's unique attributes.
