AB  - Surveyed 21 congressional staff to determine the relative effectiveness of the Mental Health Liaison Group (MHLG) and the Consortium for Citizens with Disabilities. The questionnaire was designed to seek Ss' perceptions of the effectiveness of mental health organizations relative to developmental disabilities, aging, children, and AIDS organizations. 10.5% of the Ss perceived the Washington, D.C. mental health community to be more effective than the Washington, D.C. developmental disabilities community. Many respondents noted that divisions within the mental health community undermined its influence and effectiveness. The legislators perceived the MHLG to be the most divided and least effective. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
