AB  - Studied the effects of psychological education on the mental health of impoverished undergraduates. 80 impoverished undergraduate students were randomly divided into either an intervention group or control group. The intervention group was educated on mental health for one year. The process included lecture courses, group consultation, individual consultation, and interpersonal training. Five psychological scales (SCL-90, LES, CMI SAS and SDS) were used before and after education. Compared to the control group, the intervention group showed better results on all five scales after education. It is concluded that psychological education can improve the mental health of undergraduates. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
