AB  - In this clinical essay, we describe the experience of creating and delivering a group for men with eating disorders. We outline our motivation for developing a therapeutic intervention of this nature and describe the format that we established. We then focus on the dynamics of the group that evolved and the themes that emerged in relation to issues of masculinity. We consider implications and recommendations for people interested in establishing groups for men with eating difficulties. [Reprinted by permission of Sage Publications Inc., copyright holder.]
