AB  - The article reports that the Substance Abuse and Mental Health Services Administration (SAMHSA) last week unveiled a comprehensive guide on the use of group therapy in the treatment of substance use disorders. The consensus panel that created "Substance Abuse Treatment: Group Therapy," emphasized that group therapy is effective treatment and is a cost-effective way to deliver treatment. The consensus panel found that group therapy offers a number of advantages to patients, including positive peer support, a reduction in their sense of isolation, real-life examples of people in recovery, and help from peers in coping with substance abuse and other life problems.
