AB  - The effects of brief group psychotherapy on relapse prevention are explored, comparing a group of 300 patients at 4 outpatient alcohol rehabilitation centers in Stockholm, Sweden, with a control group of alcoholics treated by other methods. Topics covered over the course of the 8-week therapy included assessing & coping with risk situations for alcohol consumption, coping with consequences of drinking, short- & long-term alternatives to drinking, & discussion of members' goals & feedback. Questionnaire & interview data obtained from 35 patients 12 months after therapy reveal no deterioration of drinking patterns. Ss' responses suggest that the leader's encouragement of personal decision making & coping skills, as well as the group structure, were responsibile for positive treatment effects. 5 Tables, 42 References. Adapted from the source document.
