AB  - The treatment of chemically dependent patients often fails due to a lack of clinically based criteria for the appropriate referral for a treatment program. A framework for categorizing chemical abuse patients is suggested, along with a drug-free treatment decision chart based on these categories. The categories spring from a dominant chemical abuse explanation, ranging from those who are self-medicating a significant & pre-existing (before chemical abuse) psychiatric disorder, to those belonging to the addictive disease group, developing significant chemical abuse problems in adulthood. Other categories include the chemically dependent who also manifest antisocial behavior, & a mixed group exhibiting fragile personality disorder, or who are narcissistic or borderline. For each group, a modality of treatment is matched with various options: inpatients or outpatient psychotherapy, pharmacotherapy, Alcoholics Anonymous, rehabilitation programs, outpatient drug counseling, or programs for dually diagnosed. In addition, psychotherapy types & alternatives are listed coinciding with the treatment modalities. 2 Tables, 68 References. J. Sadler
