AB  - The article focuses on a study of journals, and highlights their relevance for nurses who work with older people. The study involved a randomized control trail with 153 medically ill older people who scored above the threshold for depression or cognitive impairment on a brief screening instrument. Patients were allocated to usual care or nurse-led intervention groups. Subjects in the intervention group had significantly lower Geriatric Depression Scale scores at the 6 to 8-week follow up but other measures showed no change.
