AB  - The concept and method of a therapy group with special indication for unemployed patients in a clinic for alcohol- and medication addicts are presented. Material from SCHIFF's model of passivity and symbiosis is applied to the diagnosis and treatment of internal regressive mechanisms of unemployed addicts and to the therapy of disorders at levels of behavior, feeling and thinking. Therapy aims at helping unemployed patients to achieve an active problem solving attitude towards the difficulties of unemployment and improving their prognosis. Information about the realization of the conceptual plan follows. Some descriptive data about the participants and a follow-up study are reported. The possibilities of further evaluation are discussed.
