AB  - The article presents a discussion about trauma and self-help groups for addiction treatment. It states that self-help groups are large mutual aid movements that effectively implement peer-to-peer assistance, including addiction treatment. It focuses on single disorder 12-Step groups for chemical dependency. It mentions that there is evidence supporting the use of 12-Step groups for alcohol and other drug dependence. It emphasizes that 12-Step groups best serve the chemically dependent as opposed to those with a diagnosis of clinical abuse.
