AB  - The process of implementing the Care Programme Approach (CPA) in a community-based psychiatric rehabilitation team in Cambridge, England, in 1990 is described. Details of the operational policy & procedures are given, together with data describing the client group (N = 91) & examining the match between levels of mental disability & levels of services received. A relationship was found between levels of disability, type of living situation, frequency of contact with care coordinator, & frequency of contact with main carer. No relationship was found with frequency of attendance for day care or contact with closest relative. 4 Tables, 25 References. Adapted from the source document.
