AB  - The relationship among alcohol consumption & levels of treatment & self-help, health promotion, & alcohol control measures was examined through analysis of a variety of secondary source data from Ontario for the period 1975-1990. Per capita alcohol consumption decreased 19.1% during this period, & was associated with even more precipitous declines in a variety of alcohol problems. Simultaneously, physical availability of alcohol increased during the period, though economic availability remained stable. Large increases in participation in formal alcohol treatment & Alcoholics Anonymous groups occurred, & workplaces with employee assistance programs increased over tenfold; alcohol education programs for students increased by 44%. The relative importance of treatment & prevention programs in decreasing alcohol use is discussed. 4 Tables, 22 References. Adapted from the source document.
