AB  - Conducted 2 experiments to assess acquisition and generalization of skills acquired in a workshop by trainees who were primary caregivers on the staffs of group homes for developmentally disabled clients. In Exp 1, 31 staff trainees (STs [21–60 yrs old]) received a 1-wk workshop in behavioral theory and treatment techniques. When assessed at the workshop site, these STs showed increased treatment skills relative to 18 STs who did not participate in the workshop. In Exp 2, pre- and postworkshop observations were taken on 53 developmentally disabled clients (11–34 yrs old) in group homes where the STs worked. These observations provided no evidence that the workshop had any effect on group home client functioning. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
