AB  - Women represent the fastest growing population of prison inmates, which has increased dramatically in the past decade. Generally, women use more health services than men but with limited access to health care, incarcerated women tend to experience multiple problems, including problems with drugs, alcohol, & victimization. The purpose of this exploratory qualitative study was to identify specific factors related to health, mental health, drug use, & violence among incarcerated female substance users. Perspectives from 34 females who participated in focus groups in prison are discussed. Key findings indicate that drug use, victimization, & living in a rural area were barriers to accessing health services. Implications for interventions targeting women are presented. 1 Table, 34 References. Adapted from the source document.
