AB  - Observed the effects of a milieu therapy program in 80 elderly male psychiatric-medically infirm patients assigned to open, semiclosed, and closed wards. Ratings by nursing aides indicated that the functioning of Ss in the closed and semiclosed wards improved significantly over 3 mo, whereas the functioning of those in the open wards remained the same. It is concluded that the milieu therapy program was most beneficial for patients very regressed and socially deprived. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
