AB  - The art of group therapy is one that has been shown to be economical and cost effective ever since it was created. Not only is it suitable for supporting individual members to help one another alleviate pain and suffering from social problems and other personality disorders, it has also been shown to be helpful in crisis counseling. In this thesis, the Solution Focused Brief Therapy (SFBT) approach to crisis counseling is observed and helpful information regarding resiliency to overcome a crisis will also be discussed. The study included in this thesis examines how participants can employ the use of support groups to educate themselves in the art of Solution Focused Brief Therapy and in their own existing beliefs in what works to save their marriages and families in crisis. Copies of dissertations may be obtained by addressing your request to ProQuest, 789 E. Eisenhower Parkway, P.O. Box 1346, Ann Arbor, MI 48106-1346. Telephone 1-800-521-3042; email: disspub@umi.com
