AB  - The Liaison Team of the Dept of Psychiatry at Cook County Hospital (Chicago) uses a generic, multidisciplinary, crisis intervention approach to mental health consultation to facilitate humane & comprehensive yet cost-effective care for the medically indigent. Social work functions of the team include diagnosis, short-term individual & group treatment, referral, follow-up, staff development, in-service training, program planning, & interdisciplinary clinical instruction. The consultation interview & follow-up services may be a patient's first experience with a benevolent helper interested in caring for him/her as a total person & may function to humanize his/her experience in a sometimes overwhelming medical center complex located in a vast & impersonal metropolis. Modified HA.
