AB  - The treatment program studied here is set in a therapeutic community. Therapeutic communities (or TCs) have been used to treat a variety of disorders, including substance abuse (Farabee, Prendergast, & Anglin, 1998; Finney, Moos, & Chan, 1981; Hartmann, Wolk, Johnston, & Colyer, 1997) and mental illness (McMurran, Egan, & Ahmadi, 1998). The TC method of treating substance abuse involves a combination of social and psychological therapy designed to alter the client's attitudes, beliefs, and behavior. The treatment occurs in a group setting, and peer interaction is a major component of the process. Personal responsibility and mutual assistance are emphasized (Corrections Alert, 1998). (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
