AB  - The article offers focuses on a study which showed the effectiveness of a hybrid treatment called mindfulness-based cognitive therapy (MBCT) in preventing relapse in patients who have had several bouts of major depression. Zindel V. Segal, a professor of psychiatry at the University of Toronto Centre for Addiction and Mental Health, and co-author of the study, mentioned that MBCT is another treatment option for those who are unable to continue taking antidepressant medications. Researchers found that MBCT reduced the risk of relapse by 74%.
