AB  - ; The article focuses on a study of the cognitive functioning of alcoholics from the Oklahoma City Veterans Administration program for a number of years. As part of the treatment program, group testing data are collected on all patients after they have been sober for a minimum of 2 week. Alcoholic subjects who refused to participate in an extensive neuropsychological study performed less well than those who agreed to participate and those who were ineligible. The latter groups did not differ significantly in performance. Further, depression, state anxiety, the Hyperkinesis/Minimal Brain Damage scores, and vocabulary scores could not account for these findings.
